-*- mode:org -*-

accoreconsole-macos-headless-qt-blocker — --cad accoreconsole on macOS: alfe now attempts it, but AcCoreConsole aborts bootstrap before READY (Qt init)
=====================================================================================================================================================

Status: alfe side DONE (discovery + DETECT); BLOCKED on an Autodesk-internal
AcCoreConsole limitation on macOS. Found while exercising --cad accoreconsole
on the macOS runner (thalassa, real AutoCAD 2026 + 2027 installed, UNLICENSED).

Context
-------

The macOS AutoCAD bundle ships AcCoreConsole (the batch engine) even though the
AutoCAD GUI is Windows-only:

  /Applications/Autodesk/AutoCAD 2027/AutoCAD 2027.app/Contents/Helpers/AcCoreConsole.app/Contents/MacOS/AcCoreConsole

pjb confirmed AcCoreConsole launches on macOS without an immediate license
rejection, so `alfe --cad accoreconsole --mode batch' on macOS is worth
supporting. `--list-cad-programs' already discovers accoreconsole-2026 /
accoreconsole-2027 there.

What was fixed on the alfe side (this issue's branch, feat-accoreconsole-macos)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Before: `--cad accoreconsole' on macOS died IMMEDIATELY with
`alfe AUTOCAD backend error (phase DETECT): AutoCAD is not distributed for
macOS' — the autocad backend DETECT hard-refused any non-Windows host.

1. discover-accoreconsole-binary grows macOS candidates
   (macos-accoreconsole-candidates: the AcCoreConsole path inside the AutoCAD
   .app bundle, version-descending).
2. DETECT no longer refuses non-Windows outright: the GUI / COM-automation path
   stays Windows-only, but a non-Windows host is allowed when an accoreconsole
   BATCH engine is available. (Test updated to the new contract.)
   apply-cad-selection already exports the resolved path as
   $AUTOCAD_ACCORECONSOLE, which DETECT honours OS-independently, so `--cad
   accoreconsole' now reaches the engine.

The remaining blocker (Autodesk-internal, not alfe)
---------------------------------------------------

With those changes, on the macOS runner accoreconsole is launched:

  AcCoreConsole /i <writable seed.dwg> /s <workdir>/run.scr

and gets FURTHER than DETECT, but exits (exit 0) before publishing READY:

  alfe[warn]: backend AUTOCAD: process exited after 3.79 s; last status = "BOOTING"
  alfe: ... AutoCAD process exited before READY (exit 0):
        Attribute Qt::AA_PluginApplication must be set before QCoreApplication is created.
  AcCoreConsole: StdOutConsoleMode: processed-output: enabled,auto
  AutoCAD Core Engine Console - Copyright 2026 Autodesk, Inc.  ... (X.60.M.171)
  Version Number: X.60.M.171 (UNICODE)
  LogFilePath has been set to the working folder.
  .
  ; error: File load canceled: .../run-common.lsp

Observations:
  - AcCoreConsole STARTS and prints its banner — NO license rejection in the
    first ~4 s (matches pjb's manual observation).
  - It emits `Qt::AA_PluginApplication must be set before QCoreApplication is
    created' and then cancels the run.scr's (load run-common.lsp), quitting
    before READY. AA_PluginApplication is set via QCoreApplication::setAttribute
    inside AcCoreConsole's OWN startup — not settable from the environment, so
    QT_QPA_PLATFORM etc. do not address it.
  - Two intermediate blockers already handled while probing: (a) the bundle
    .dwt templates are READ-ONLY ("currently in use or is read-only") — feed a
    WRITABLE copy; (b) the backend's template discovery
    (candidate-autocad-template-paths) looks NEXT TO the binary, wrong for the
    deeply-nested macOS AcCoreConsole — macOS templates live under
    .../Contents/Resources/UserDataCache/<locale>/Template/*.dwt.

Next steps / open questions
---------------------------

- Is the Qt::AA_PluginApplication abort inherent to running AcCoreConsole
  outside the AutoCAD app on macOS, or does a specific launch context /
  entitlement / working directory avoid it? (Needs Autodesk-side knowledge or
  experimentation on the macOS box.)
- If AcCoreConsole can be made to reach READY, add macOS template discovery to
  candidate-autocad-template-paths (Resources/UserDataCache/<locale>/Template)
  and copy the chosen template to a writable per-run drawing, so batch mode
  works without an explicit --dwg.
- Decide whether to SHIP the DETECT relaxation before the engine works: it
  turns a clean "unsupported on macOS" into an attempt that fails at bootstrap.
  Kept on feat-accoreconsole-macos (draft) pending this decision.

Repro (macOS with AutoCAD installed)
------------------------------------

  alfe --cad accoreconsole --mode batch --dwg <writable.dwg> -x '(princ "HI")'
  # -> AcCoreConsole starts, Qt::AA_PluginApplication, exits before READY.


PARKED — confirmed an Autodesk macOS AcCoreConsole bug (2026-08-02, pjb, thalassa)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

With the --cad DETECT fix (1.7.12) alfe now reaches AcCoreConsole on macOS.
Empirically the engine is NOT usable there yet, on BOTH installed versions:

  - AutoCAD 2027 AcCoreConsole  X.60.M.171
  - AutoCAD 2026 AcCoreConsole  W.119.M.325

Both, with AND without QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen, print
"Attribute Qt::AA_PluginApplication must be set before QCoreApplication is
created." and then CANCEL every LISP load — decisively including AUTODESK's OWN
startup lisp (acad2027.LSP / acad2026.LSP), not just our run-common.lsp. So this
is Autodesk's binary, not our code or a trust issue we introduced; exit code is
0 (no license wall). QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen has no effect (the fault is the
AA_PluginApplication *attribute*, set in C++ before QCoreApplication, not the
platform plugin).

Contributing but secondary: "File load canceled" is also the classic headless
SECURELOAD / Trusted-Locations symptom (a temp-dir .lsp triggers a trust prompt
a headless engine can't answer). Even fixing that would not help while Autodesk's
own startup lisp dies on the Qt error.

Decision: PARK macOS AcCoreConsole. Real AutoCAD conformance runs on Windows
(green). Keep the --cad access (opt-in via $AUTOCAD_ACCORECONSOLE, which --cad
sets) to re-test on a fixed Autodesk build. Worth an Autodesk report.

Useful nuggets for the capture work IF the Qt bug ever clears: AcCoreConsole
prints "Redirect stdout (file: /var/tmp/accc……)" — it already tees its stdout to
a temp file — and "LogFilePath has been set to the working folder" (LOGFILEPATH
works). Both are alternative capture paths worth revisiting then. See
[[autocad-no-rest-output-capture]].
